# AGENTS.md

## Project Identity

This workspace is a generated multi-page React admin application titled `{{TITLE}}`.

## Runtime Stack

- React
- Material UI v6
- Material React Table for rich admin tables
- React Router
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Vitest
- pnpm

## Local Structure

- `src/router.tsx` defines the route structure.
- `src/Layout.tsx`, `src/Header.tsx`, and `src/Sidebar.tsx` define the app shell.
- `src/pages/` contains page-level routes for `{{PAGES}}`.

## Working Rules

- Prefer incremental changes over broad rewrites.
- Keep app-shell changes aligned across Header, Sidebar, and routed pages.
- Keep rich admin tables on Material React Table unless a page is clearly a simple static table.
- Put reusable visual decisions in the theme/provider layer instead of scattering overrides.
- Do not confuse this workspace `AGENTS.md` with `.github/agents/*`; this file documents the local project, not the Copilot bundle.

## Validation

- For layout or route changes, verify navigation and page rendering before broader checks.
- For page-level data-table changes, verify filtering, pagination, row actions, and UI states.
- Start validation with `pnpm typecheck`.
- Add `pnpm test` when behavior changes or existing tests cover the touched scope.
- Add `pnpm build` only when production output, routing, provider setup, or build configuration changed.

## Nested AGENTS

- Add nested `AGENTS.md` files only when a page group or sub-app grows into a genuinely different boundary, such as a legacy area or a dedicated domain package.
